WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.236
Third Normal Form removes transitive dependencies
Even

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:07.907
after separating appointment and service facts we

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.907
should not keep patient name and provider

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.301
specialty inside every appointment row if those

00:00:12.328 --> 00:00:14.722
values are determined by patient or provider

00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:19.075
identifiers The appointment should store the foreign

00:00:19.101 --> 00:00:21.654
keys that identify the patient and provider

00:00:23.395 --> 00:00:27.700
Patient details belong in patient Provider details

00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:31.745
belong in provider A common memory aid

00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:34.192
for 3NF is that non-key facts should

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:35.903
describe the key and should not really

00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:40.328
depend on another non-key attribute The practical

00:00:40.354 --> 00:00:43.843
benefit is easier maintenance If a provider's

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.725
specialty changes we update the provider record

00:00:46.751 --> 00:00:48.528
rather than many appointment rows
